 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** $O(1)$ per face. The calculation involves a fixed number of arithmetic operations and array lookups, independent of scene complexity or distance [G].
+*   **Time Complexity:** $O(1)$ per face [G]. The calculation involves a fixed number of arithmetic operations and array lookups, independent of scene complexity or distance [G].
 *   **Memory Complexity:** $O(1)$ additional memory per face, aside from the static lookup tables for block properties and noise generators [G].
 *   **Performance:** Extremely fast, suitable for real-time rendering of massive voxel worlds on CPU or GPU without the overhead of ray marching or shadow map generation [G].
 *   **Strengths:** Deterministic, easy to implement, no artifacts from ray marching step counts, no memory bandwidth issues associated with shadow maps [G].
-*   **Limitations:** Shadows do not correspond to actual geometry (a block far away can cast a "shadow" on a nearby block if coordinates align). Shadows do not change with light position or time (unless coordinates are time-dependent). No soft shadows or penumbrae [G].
+*   **Limitations:** Shadows do not correspond to actual geometry (a block far away can cast a "shadow" on a nearby block if coordinates align) [G]. Shadows do not change with light position or time (unless coordinates are time-dependent) [G]. No soft shadows or penumbrae [G].
 *   **When to use:** Stylized voxel games, procedural terrain generation where performance is critical, or as a fallback when physical accuracy is not required [G].
 *   **When not to use:** Realistic rendering, scenes with dynamic moving light sources, or when accurate occlusion is required for gameplay mechanics [G].
